SUMMARY:Enterprise AI in the Physical World: Navigating the Supply Chain
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nIn this session of *Newsweek’s* “AI 
 Impact Forum\,” **Dr. Ranjit Tinaikar** speaks with **Duncan Angove**\, 
 chief executive officer of Blue Yonder\, about bringing enterprise AI into
  warehouses\, factories\, transportation networks and other environments w
 here digital decisions have immediate real-world consequences.\nAngove des
 cribes supply chain as a “messy frontier” for AI\, shaped by constant 
 movement\, unpredictable edge cases and institutional knowledge built thro
 ugh years of human experience. The conversation will examine how companies
  can combine general-purpose AI with specialized models designed for speci
 fic operational tasks\, while preserving the expertise that distinguishes 
 how their businesses run.\nTinaikar and Angove will also explore what incr
 easingly autonomous systems could mean for the economics of enterprise tec
 hnology. That includes whether companies begin focusing less on software s
 eats or AI consumption and more on measurable outcomes such as moving good
 s faster\, improving productivity and lowering operating costs.\nThe discu
 ssion will extend to the people operating alongside these systems: how com
 panies build trust\, manage adoption and use AI to augment the judgment an
 d experience required in complex frontline work.\n\nDesigned for CEOs\, su
 pply chain and operations leaders\, technology executives and other senior
  decision-makers\, the session will offer a practical look at how AI is ch
 anging the systems and decisions behind the movement of goods through the 
 global economy.\n\nRegister here: https://app.sequel.io/newsweek/duncan-an
 gove-blue-yonder-supply-chain-ai
